        <referenceFunction amount="1.0" category="metals" datasetRelatesToProduct="true" generalComment="The module describes the global production mix for jointly produced zinc- and lead-concentrates from  sulphidic deposits. The multioutput-process “exploitation, zinc-lead-deposit” delivers the three co-products “lead, concentrate, at beneficiation” and “zinc, concentrate, at beneficiation”. It is designed for the use of the concentrates as raw material for the ultimate production of lead and zinc.;&#10;UUID: 4b7c911d-f95a-3d99-a16c-389eaf259c0d" includedProcesses="The module includes the mining and the beneficiation step with the mining infrastructure and disposal of overburden and tailings (see part &quot;Auxiliary Processes&quot;)." infrastructureProcess="false" localCategory="metals" localName="Zinc concentrate, at beneficiation" localSubCategory="non ferro" name="Zinc concentrate, at beneficiation" subCategory="non ferro" unit="kg"/>
        <geography location="GLO" text="&lt;null&gt;"/>
        <technology text="This module is approximated with values from nickel-mining. Mining is assumed to be underground, followed by froth beneficiation. Overburden and tailings are disposed inside the mining panels. For electricity mix a mix of 25% coal and 75% gas fired plants was chosen."/>
